# --- Python & Backend ---
#
# The setuptools build-artifact names below are ANCHORED with a leading slash,
# which restricts each to the repo root and to backend/. Unanchored, git
# matches a directory of that name at *any* depth — and `lib/` therefore
# matched `frontend/src/lib/`, silently ignoring the frontend's entire data
# layer. The files already committed there stayed tracked (an ignore rule does
# not affect tracked files), so nothing looked wrong; only *new* ones vanished.
# `src/lib/routes.ts` was added and never staged, and since `proxy.ts` — the
# auth guard — imports it, a fresh clone would have failed to build on an
# unresolved module. Add new paths here anchored, never bare.
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*$py.class
*.so
.Python
/build/
/backend/build/
/develop-eggs/
/backend/develop-eggs/
/dist/
/backend/dist/
/downloads/
/eggs/
/backend/eggs/
/.eggs/
/backend/.eggs/
/lib/
/backend/lib/
/lib64/
/backend/lib64/
/parts/
/sdist/
/backend/sdist/
/var/
/wheels/
/backend/wheels/
/share/python-wheels/
*.egg-info/
.installed.cfg
*.egg
MANIFEST
*.manifest
*.spec

# --- Virtual Environments & Package Managers ---
.venv/
env/
venv/
ENV/
env.bak/
venv.bak/
.uv/
.ruff_cache/
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/

# --- Environment Variables & Secrets ---
.env
.env.local
.env.*.local

# --- Frontend & Node ---
node_modules/
.next/
out/
dist-ssr/
*.local

# --- IDE & OS specific ---
.vscode/
.idea/
*.suo
*.ntvs*
*.njsproj
*.sln
*.swp
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# --- Logs & Databases ---
*.log
logs/
*.sqlite3
*.db